A game's sound follows the Mac's default output (AirPods, headphones, a display's speakers) while it plays.

This repository's patch to winecoreaudio (version 1), on top of 0009 and 0038, to be offered to WineHQ. It is
mavrik's own; nothing is copied. Its shape is upstream Wine's own on Linux, and its mechanism is OpenAL Soft's on the
Mac:
- winepulse.drv lists a first endpoint with an empty device name ("PulseAudio Output") as the default; a stream on
  it connects to PulseAudio's default sink and moves with it, and a stream on a named sink is opened with
  PA_STREAM_DONT_MOVE (dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c, pulse_test_connect and pulse_connect_stream). winealsa.drv
  does the same with ALSA's "default" device (dlls/winealsa.drv/alsa.c, get_endpoint_ids).
- OpenAL Soft's CoreAudio backend opens kAudioUnitSubType_DefaultOutput, Apple's output unit that tracks the
  default device, when no device is named, and kAudioUnitSubType_HALOutput for a named one
  (alc/backends/coreaudio.cpp, CoreAudioPlayback::open).
Wine bugs 54779 and 55970 report the fault (open; a Wine developer suggested listening for system output changes).

Before: winecoreaudio bound each stream to the device that was the default when the stream was made (a
kAudioUnitSubType_HALOutput unit with kAudioOutputUnitProperty_CurrentDevice set), and mmdevapi fixed its default
endpoint when the process started. Connecting AirPods left the game on the speakers; a device that went away
(AirPods put back in the case) left the game silent until it was restarted.

Now winecoreaudio lists "System Default Output" (and "System Default Input") first, as the default endpoint, with
an empty device string, followed by every device as before. A render stream on it uses
kAudioUnitSubType_DefaultOutput with no device set, so macOS moves it to each new default output, including the one
macOS picks when the default device disappears. A stream on a named device stays on that device, as on Windows.
The empty device string resolves to the current default device for the mix format, the format check and the
device period, and a following stream reads its unit's current device for its latency and volume. A capture stream
on the default endpoint opens on the default input of the moment and stays there. mmdevapi is unchanged.

Windows: high-level APIs (DirectSound, XAudio2, winmm, Media Foundation) move a stream to the new default since
Windows 7, and WASAPI streams activated on the default interface since Windows 10 1607 ("Automatic stream routing",
learn.microsoft.com). In Wine all of these open the default endpoint through mmdevapi, so all of them follow. A raw
WASAPI stream opened on GetDefaultAudioEndpoint's device follows here too, as it does under winepulse;
IMMNotificationClient::OnDefaultDeviceChanged is not sent, since Wine's default endpoint never changes.

Checked (mavrik S222 lab): applies after patches 0001 to 0042 with no fuzz; winecoreaudio.so builds with the
engine's toolchain and configure line with no warning (the same tree without this patch rebuilt revision 12's
winecoreaudio.so byte for byte). Its live check (a WASAPI program while the default output changes and while it
disappears, against revision 12) is the lab's next step.
